# Every model file Riffsheet ships, with its digest and where it came from.
#
# shell/cmake/ReleaseAudit.cmake refuses to build a release if a file under this
# directory is missing from this list, if a digest does not match, or if a line
# here names a file that is not there. That is what stops non-redistributable
# weights being dropped into Resources/ and shipped by accident.
#
# nmp.onnx  -  Spotify Basic Pitch, Apache-2.0. Byte-for-byte the file at
#              basic_pitch/saved_models/icassp_2022/nmp.onnx in spotify/basic-pitch
#              v0.4.0 (model blob added in commit dfb20ef559dff1792e11e022f3f0c7008c1dee6d;
#              git blob sha1 c30e5f9438e798604b7177aa26be1fe64482f767). Unmodified.
#              Licence text ships at third-party/basic-pitch/LICENSE.
#
# beat-this/small0.onnx  -  CPJKU Beat This!, MIT, code AND published weights.
#              The repository's README says so in as many words: "The code and the
#              published model weights are released under the MIT license." (It
#              adds that some TRAINING files are copyrighted, which is a statement
#              about the data, not about the weights.) That is the licence gate of
#              engine-architecture.md section 6.6 answered from the project itself,
#              not from a summary; the text ships at third-party/beat-this/LICENSE.
#
#              It is the `small0` checkpoint - 2.1 M parameters - and NOT `final0`,
#              which is 20.3 M and 77 MB of fp32 weights: three products x 77 MB
#              blows both the 35 MB per-product and the 100 MB bundle budget on its
#              own. The accuracy paid for that is in NOTICE.md and BUILDING.md.
#
#              Riffsheet EXPORTED this file; there is no official ONNX release. It
#              is torch.onnx.export of beat_this 1.1.0's BeatThis module loaded
#              from beat_this-small0.ckpt (sha256
#              6074be2c4d490c5f6101fcc374a1ec72ae93456e23bb6019783b849f5dc7d47b -
#              recorded again in shell/test/golden/beats-clicks.json, which is the
#              digest the golden was captured with), opset 17, dynamic time. The
#              exact invocation is in BUILDING.md section 5 so it can be repeated.
#
# Format is sha256sum's, so it can be checked by hand:
#     cd shell/Resources/models && shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256
2c3c1d144bfa61ad236e92e169c13535c880469a12a047d4e73451f2c059a0ec  basic-pitch/nmp.onnx
9fa72ac17486ae137ee05ad0ef6a3dba63001c5aa6ada1ecb81c819870d67713  beat-this/small0.onnx
